## B. Sentinel-1 SAR Preprocessing Comparison

### Scripts Audited
| Script | Author | Lines | Reader | Norm Mode |
|:-------|:-------|------:|:-------|:----------|
| `sar_preprocessing_meet.py` | Meet | 385 | rasterio → PIL fallback | Configurable: none/min-max/**z-score** |
| `sar_preprocessing_adarsh.py` | Adarsh | 331 | rasterio → PIL fallback | Z-score only |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` | Fateh | 331 | PIL only (rasterio fallback inline) | Z-score only |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh_2.py`* | Fateh | 45 | PIL only | Per-band Z-score (no population stats) |

*`sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` = clean production version; `sar_preprocessing_fateh_2.py` = the one actually named `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` in `weeks/week_02/preprocessing/` is the 45-line version — see below.

### B1. VV/VH Band Selection & Order

All four implementations: Channel 0 = VV, Channel 1 = VH. ✅ Fully consistent.

### B2. dB Clipping

| Script | VV Clip | VH Clip | Validation |
|:-------|:--------|:--------|:-----------|
| `sar_preprocessing_meet.py` | [-25.0, 0.0] configurable via `VV_CLIP_RANGE` | [-25.0, 0.0] configurable | ✅ `min < max` check |
| `sar_preprocessing_adarsh.py` | [-25.0, 0.0] hardcoded constants | [-25.0, 0.0] | ✅ `min < max` check |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (331-line) | [-25.0, 0.0] hardcoded constants | [-25.0, 0.0] | ✅ `min < max` check |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (45-line actual file) | ❌ **No clipping** | ❌ **No clipping** | — |

> [!CAUTION]
> **The 45-line `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (actual file on disk) skips dB clipping entirely.** It reads bands, resizes, and applies per-band normalization with no `np.clip` call. This will pass extreme outlier dB values into the model.

### B3. Normalization

| Script | Method | Stats Source | Per-band or joint |
|:-------|:-------|:-------------|:-----------------|
| `sar_preprocessing_meet.py` | Z-score `(clipped - mean) / std` | `s1_stats.json` via `config.settings` | Per-band (VV and VH separately) |
| `sar_preprocessing_adarsh.py` | Z-score `(clipped - mean) / std` | `s1_stats.json` from `parent.parent` | Per-band |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (331-line) | Z-score `(clipped - mean) / std` | `s1_stats.json` from `parent` | Per-band |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (45-line, actual) | **Per-patch** `(x - x_mean) / x_std` | Each patch's own pixels | Spatial mean over H×W |

The 45-line version also does not load `s1_stats.json` at all — no population stats used.

### B4. Transformation Pipeline Comparison

```
meet/adarsh/fateh(331):  Load → Clip[-25,0] → Z-score(population stats) → Resize(224) → Stack → Tensor
fateh(45-line actual):   Load → Resize(224) → Stack → Per-patch Z-score → Tensor   [NO CLIP]
```

### B5. NaN/Inf Validation

| Script | Finite check |
|:-------|:------------|
| `sar_preprocessing_meet.py` | ✅ After normalization; raises ValueError |
| `sar_preprocessing_adarsh.py` | ✅ After normalization + final tensor |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (331-line) | ✅ Same as Adarsh |
| `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (45-line) | ❌ None |

### B6. SAR Canonical Candidate

**`sar_preprocessing_adarsh.py`** ⭐ (nearly identical to `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` 331-line, which is structurally identical)

The two are functionally equivalent except for `STATS_PATH` location. `sar_preprocessing_meet.py` is more configurable but requires `config.settings` import. For the canonical selection, **either Adarsh or Fateh's 331-line version** works best — they are virtually the same code. Meet's version is preferred if `config.settings` is centralized first.

> **Important**: The 45-line `sar_preprocessing_fateh.py` (the actual file on disk) is a simplified/incomplete version and must **not** be used in the training pipeline.

