### C2. SAR-MS Pairing Mechanism

All three use the same CSV-driven pairing: `train_split.csv` has columns `s1_name`, `s2v1_name`, `patch_id`. S1 patch directory is located via a JSON cache built by scanning `s1_root`. S2 folder is resolved via 4-candidate path search. **Pairing is deterministic and correct** given valid CSV. ✅

### C3. Split Isolation

`PairedBigEarthNetDataset` uses one CSV per split (train/val/test) — no cross-contamination possible. `BigEarthNetS1Dataset` uses a split file (`.txt`) or deterministic 70/15/15 fallback with seed=42. ✅ Split integrity preserved.

