## D. End-to-End Pipeline Compatibility

```
Raw S1 (120×120, Float32 dB) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  ↓ load VV + VH via rasterio (or PIL fallback)                                             │
  ↓ clip to [-25, 0] dB                                                                     │
  ↓ z-score per band: (x - VV_mean) / VV_std                                               │
  ↓ resize 120×120 → 224×224 bilinear                                                       │  Dataset.__getitem__
  ↓ stack [VV, VH] → Tensor (2, 224, 224) float32 ─────────────────────────────────────────┤
                                                                                             │
Raw S2 (120×120, DN float32) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
  ↓ read B04, B03, B02 TIFFs via rasterio (or PIL)                                         │ │
  ↓ resize 120×120 → 224×224 bilinear                                                       │ │
  ↓ z-score per channel: (x - CH_mean) / CH_std using s2_stats.json                        │ │
  ↓ Tensor (3, 224, 224) float32 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ │
                                                                                             │ │
CSV (patch_id, s1_name, s2v1_name, labels) ─────────────────────────────────────────────── ↓ ↓
  → PairedBigEarthNetDataset.__getitem__ → (SAR tensor, MS tensor, label (19,), patch_id)
  → DataLoader (batch_size=64, shuffle=True) → collate_fn
  → Batch: SAR (64,2,224,224) + MS (64,3,224,224) + Labels (64,19) + patch_ids[64]
  → Two-Tower ResNet-50 × 2 → 512-D embeddings → InfoNCE loss
```

**Compatible combinations**: Meet's SAR + Meet's S2 + Meet's Dataset + Meet's DataLoader ✅  
**Broken combinations**: Any script using `from week4.xxx` imports when run from `weeks/week_02/` ❌

